>> title: Osso Buco
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: veal, italian, wine, oven, braise
>> counters: Pizzeria, One Pot
>> aka: ossobuco, osso buco alla milanese, braised veal shanks
>> servings: 4
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: narrow — two hours keeps the shank on the bone; at three the meat lets go and what you have is a good ragù instead
>> washing-up: the Dutch oven, a shallow dish to dredge the shanks in

Preheat the #oven{} to 325°F (160°C).

Dredge @veal shanks{4}(3 lb / 1.4 kg total, tied), @all-purpose flour{1/3%cup}(40 g), @kosher salt{2%tsp} in a shallow #dish{}.

Brown @&(~1)floured shanks{}, @unsalted butter{3%Tbs} in a #Dutch oven{}.

Soften @yellow onion{1%large}(finely chopped), @carrot{1%large}(finely chopped), @celery{2%ribs}(finely chopped) with @&(~1)browned shanks{}.

>> step: braise 325°F 2 hr
Braise @&(~1)pot{} with @dry white wine{1%cup}(240 mL), @chicken stock{2%cup}(475 mL) for ~{2%hr}.

Chop @lemon zest{1%Tbs}, @flat-leaf parsley{1/4%cup}, @garlic{1%clove} to a gremolata.

>> step: scatter over
Scatter @&(~1)gremolata{} over @&(~2)osso buco{}.
